From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] user32, samlib: what Windows 7's Start menu needs

Purpose: let Windows 7's Start menu open, and let DirectUser do its
deferred work (layout and painting) while its threads wait for messages.
Windows 7 behavior: the taskbar builds the Start menu ("DV2ControlHost",
title "スタート メニュー") with its panes. The search pane ("Desktop OpenBox
Host") creates the "Search Box" window and then looks up
user32.RegisterMessagePumpHook with GetProcAddress; when it is missing,
the pane's WM_CREATE returns -1 and the whole menu is destroyed, so the
Start button does nothing. shacct.dll, which delay-loads samlib, calls
SamConnect on the taskbar thread. DirectUser (duser.dll) registers the
hook on each of its threads and returns its own functions for the five
user32 message calls it imports (GetMessage, PeekMessage, WaitMessage,
GetQueueStatus and MsgWaitForMultipleObjectsEx): a structure of 40 bytes
on x64 with all four addresses set. It finishes deferred work in them, for
example a folder window's icons once they are extracted.
Wine before: user32 had no RegisterMessagePumpHook or
UnregisterMessagePumpHook, and samlib only had stubs ("unimplemented
function samlib.dll.SamConnect", an exception the caller catches).
Change: RegisterMessagePumpHook calls the hook with the addresses of
user32's own message functions (GetMessage/PeekMessage, a wait, the queue
status and MsgWaitForMultipleObjectsEx), keeps the addresses the hook
returns and counts registrations; UnregisterMessagePumpHook calls the hook
with TRUE when the count reaches zero. As in ReactOS (dwcPumpHook), each
registration also counts for the calling thread: on a thread that
registered it, GetMessageW, PeekMessageW, WaitMessage, GetQueueStatus and
MsgWaitForMultipleObjectsEx (and the functions built on them) call the
hook's functions, which call user32's own; other threads are not
affected. A function the hook leaves empty stays user32's own. SamConnect returns
STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED (there is no SAM), SamCloseHandle and SamFreeMemory
succeed. Signatures and the structure follow ReactOS's user32 and samlib.
Evidence: with the change the Start button opens the Start menu with the
programs list, "すべてのプログラム", the search box, the right column and the
shut down button; SamConnect is called twice and the caller goes on.
Routing on every thread called DirectUser's functions on threads it had
not set up (a call to address 0); per thread, the Computer folder shows
its drive and Control Panel icons and the drives' free space bars as
soon as they are ready, which without routing showed only after an input
event.
Scope: new exports, and the message functions of threads that registered
a message pump hook. XP's and ReactOS's shell modules do not register one.
